{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\UserRightsOverview\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-shadows-server",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "psr/http-message 2.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 34",
        "psr/log 3.0.2, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 34"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "vendor/ ships 2 packages that the server ships itself in a major of Nextcloud 31 to 34. Both copies define the same classes, and the autoloader that is asked first decides which version runs.",
        "  psr/http-message 2.0, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 34",
        "  psr/log 3.0.2, in 3rdparty/ of Nextcloud 31 to 34"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ocp-deprecated",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Service/GroupFoldersService.php:30 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isInstalled(): deprecated since Nextcloud 32; Use either self::isEnabledForUser or self::isEnabledForAnyone"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 use in 1 file of the public API that is deprecated in Nextcloud 31 to 34. The text of the tag names the replacement where it has one.",
        "  lib/Service/GroupFoldersService.php:30 OCP\\App\\IAppManager::isInstalled(): deprecated since Nextcloud 32; Use either self::isEnabledForUser or self::isEnabledForAnyone"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "job-time-sensitivity",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/BackgroundJob/MonthlyReportJob.php OCA\\UserRightsOverview\\BackgroundJob\\MonthlyReportJob"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 timed job does not say whether it is time sensitive. A job that sets TIME_INSENSITIVE with setTimeSensitivity() is moved to the maintenance window of the server; whether a job is heavy enough for that only its maintainer knows.",
        "  lib/BackgroundJob/MonthlyReportJob.php OCA\\UserRightsOverview\\BackgroundJob\\MonthlyReportJob"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "time-direct",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/BackgroundJob/MonthlyReportJob.php:48 new DateTime()"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "lib/ reads the clock directly in 1 place. OCP\\AppFramework\\Utility\\ITimeFactory, a PSR-20 ClockInterface, gives the same time and can be replaced in a test.",
        "  lib/BackgroundJob/MonthlyReportJob.php:48 new DateTime()"
      ]
    },
